WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
One new sound today. And then your child reads real words.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:10.912
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:13.992
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:16.328
Old sounds first. All six.

5
00:00:17.664 --> 00:00:18.529
As in nest.

6
00:00:23.711 --> 00:00:24.657
Now the new one.

7
00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:28.603
As in moon. Draw a curved moon in the air.

8
00:00:30.337 --> 00:00:36.403
This sound and the one from day four are easy to mix up by ear. So let your child watch your mouth.

9
00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:38.613
As in moon.

10
00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:41.015
As in nest.

11
00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:47.521
For moon, the lips are shut. For nest, the lips are open, and the tongue is up behind the top teeth.

12
00:00:47.971 --> 00:00:54.327
Now the words. Each letter has a dot under it. Touch a dot, say its sound. Then slide them together.

13
00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:57.620
The word is at.

14
00:01:02.124 --> 00:01:03.140
The word is man.

15
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:09.371
Read the first word together. Then press play on your child's listening track, and step away.

16
00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:16.306
The voice waits, then says each sound and the word, so your child can check it alone. Nothing listens back.

17
00:01:16.756 --> 00:01:23.425
If joining the sounds is hard today, that is fine. The sounds are today's job. The words are a first taste.

18
00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:26.387
At the end, your child reads three words to you.
